'' 'w &= x' OVER A FIXED WIDE STRING, and what x may be. Only a wide VARIABLE worked:
'' the source was asked for its ADDRESS, so every call declined -- 'w &= wstr( "2" )'
'' and 'w &= trim( w2 )' alike -- and a narrow, numeric or boolean source declined
'' outright. Measured, each shape separately:
''
''   w &= w2      fb_WstrConcatAssign( W, 80, W2 )
''   w &= "lit"   TMP = fb_WstrConcatWA( W, (void*)"lit", 4 ); fb_WstrAssign( W, 80,
''                TMP ); fb_WstrDelete( TMP )   -- an append into a TEMPORARY, assigned
''                back, not fb_WstrConcatAssign with the narrow bytes
''   w &= n       vr = fb_IntToWstr( N ); TMP = vr; fb_WstrConcatAssign( W, 80, TMP );
''                fb_WstrDelete( TMP )
''   w &= b       the same through fb_BoolToWstr, which writes "true" where
''                fb_IntToWstr would write -1 -- BOOLEAN has its own wide renderer
''                exactly as it has its own narrow one, and tiko-lang used the integer
''                one for it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/wide-append.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_BoolToWstr
'' GOLDEN: expected/wide-append.out
